  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) achieved the best accuracy so far (0.650), a large jump over singleprofile scvi_n200 (0.520) and pca_n2000 (0.485). Image-only models are weak (0.21), so RNA is the dominant signal. Uncertainty: within the multiprofile + scvi_n200 family, the only untested variable is aggregation method (transformer vs. avgpool). This experiment (config_006) isolates that single change, testing whether a transformer aggregator can further improve over avgpool. It is the best next step because it directly extends the current best result with a minimal, interpretable change, and the outcome (whether transformer > avgpool) will inform all subsequent multimodal experiments where aggregation is a key design choice. With 5 experiments remaining, establishing the optimal aggregation before moving to multimodal fusion is the most efficient use of budget."
}

